course: dictionary
lesson: 4167
title: The goatherd in the hills
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A goatherd is a person whose job is to look after goats. They take the goats out to graze, which means eating grass, usually up in the hills. Look at the clues in the sentence: «the story of a goatherd named Kaldi whose goats danced after eating the berries». The goats are the clue, so a goatherd must be someone who looks after goats.
explain: The word is made of two parts: goat and herd. A herd is a group of animals, so a goatherd is the one who looks after a herd of goats. Shepherds do the same job with sheep. In stories and Bible lessons they live simple lives tending their animals.
explain: In «Heidi», Peter is a goatherd who takes the goats up the Alps. Think about the setting: the Alps are high mountains, so a goatherd often works far from town. When you meet a new word, ask what the words around it tell you, then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: A goatherd is a person whose job is to look after goats.
fact: Goatherds usually take their goats out to graze in the hills.
fact: A shepherd looks after sheep; a goatherd looks after goats.
fact: In «Heidi», the goatherd Peter takes the goats up the Alps.
fact: Phrases: a young goatherd, the goatherd's hut.
exercise: What is a goatherd? | A person who sells milk in the town | A hut high in the mountains | A goat that leads the herd | *A person who looks after goats
exercise: «The goatherd took his goats up the hill to graze.» What does graze mean? | *To eat grass | To run very fast | To climb steep rocks | To sleep under a tree
exercise: In «Heidi», what does Peter do? | He sells coffee in the city | He builds a castle on the hill | *He takes the goats up the Alps | He sails across the sea
test: «...the story of a goatherd named Kaldi whose goats danced after eating the berries is a legend nobody can prove.» What does legend mean here? | *A famous old story that may not be true | A list of goat names | A map of the hills | A kind of coffee plant
test: In the phrase «a young goatherd», what does young tell you? | The goatherd is a goat | The goatherd lives in a city | *The goatherd is a young person | The goatherd is very old
exam: What does goatherd mean in «a goatherd named Kaldi»? | A kind of goat | A type of coffee plant | A hill with lots of grass | *A person who looks after goats
